{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-158364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(2<X\\le 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{21}{x}^{2},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{21}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{63}{x}^{3}]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{63}(27-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{63}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158364" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158364" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158364" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13}{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{14}{63}"] ["math" "\\frac{17}{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{63}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{21}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158364" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{19}{63}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(-1<X\\le 0)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}(x+2)(1-x),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1<X\\le 0) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2}{9}(x+2)(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-{x}^{2}-x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{[-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}([-\\frac{1}{3}(0)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}+2(0)]-[-\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}+2(-1)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(0-[\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}-2]) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{13}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10}{27}"] ["math" "\\frac{13}{27}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{27}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13}{27}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(1<X<2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{3},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<2) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{80}{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{80}(16-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{16}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-86913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(2<X<8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{50}x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-86913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<8) & ={\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{8}\\frac{1}{50}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{100}{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-86913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-86913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-86913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-86913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(1\\le X<2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{27}(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X<2) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{4}{27}(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}{[{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}([(2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{4}]-[(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}(8-4-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}\\cdot \\frac{13}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13}{27}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{27}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13}{27}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X>-3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2},\\, & -6\\le x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>-3) & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{216}{x}^{3}]}_{-3}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{216}[(0)^{3}-(-3)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{216} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X>-1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{28}({x}^{2}+1),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x>2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>-1) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{3}{28}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x]}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}([\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3}+(2)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}+(-1)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}([\\frac{8}{3}+2]-[-\\frac{1}{3}-1]) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158360" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158360" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{14}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{14}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{14}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158360" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{14}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X\\le -1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{35}{x}^{2},\\, & -2\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{3}{35}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{35}{x}^{3}]}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[(-1)^{3}-(-2)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}(-1+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X\\ge 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{34}({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x>3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{3}{34}({x}^{3}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{34}{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{34}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{34}([\\frac{1}{4}(3)^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3}]-[\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{34}([\\frac{81}{4}-9]-[4-\\frac{8}{3}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{34}\\cdot \\frac{119}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X\\le 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{24}({x}^{2}+1),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{24}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+x]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}[(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+3)-(\\frac{1}{3}+1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}(12-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot \\frac{32}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(0\\le X\\le 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}x(x+1),\\, & 0\\le x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}x & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{5}x(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{6}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{5}({x}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{6}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}+{[\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}([\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}(0)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}])+\\frac{1}{12}[{2}^{2}-{1}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(\\frac{5}{6})+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(2<X\\le 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}x,\\, & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 3<x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{6}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[{3}^{2}-{2}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(9-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(3<X<4)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2},\\, & -1\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}(x-1) & 1<x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X<4) & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}([\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2}-(4)]-[\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2}-(3)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(8-4-\\frac{9}{2}+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{18}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(-1\\le X\\le 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10}({x}^{2}+1),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{20} & 1<x\\le 9, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1\\le X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{10}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{20}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x]}_{-1}^{1}+{[\\frac{1}{20}x]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}([\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}+1]-[\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}+(-1)])+\\frac{1}{20}(2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\frac{8}{3})+\\frac{1}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}+\\frac{1}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{60}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158445" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158445" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13}{60}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{60}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{20}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{30}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{20}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158445" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{19}{60}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(0<X\\le 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{3}+1),\\, & -1\\le x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{24}x & 1\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{24}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+x]}_{0}^{1}+{[\\frac{1}{48}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}+1]-[\\frac{1}{4}(0)^{4}+0])+\\frac{1}{48}[{5}^{2}-{1}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{5}{4})+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{16}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc875edfe754176e0e99ef50f5a91d839b85e7925cd920fe218803e9ba0601c8"} {"question" "q-158443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{13}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "q-158443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13}{16}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/state.json" "file_sha256" "62cee77d1f5fa43b49e1eb0c1976e06b34d86ea17ec6775b241d12683125f5f7"} {"question" "e-10839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P\\left( 1 \\lt   X \\lt 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/assets/394c60a510e39043cda5072c0b57a663b200275035d72c15f20c5a257e6c4fc0.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/example-10839.json" "file_sha256" "0482ed6488823ef2cb45b0cabb894a565033e115e67078564897de8a3f675e36"} {"question" "e-10839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\lt   X \\lt      b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{18}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{\\int }_{1}^{3}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-x]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}([\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3}-(3)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}-(1)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}([9-3]-[\\frac{1}{3}-1]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}(6+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}\\cdot \\frac{20}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/example-10839.json" "file_sha256" "0482ed6488823ef2cb45b0cabb894a565033e115e67078564897de8a3f675e36"} {"question" "e-11036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P\\left(  X \\leq 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/assets/1cd6271fdb46d54db66d2b4f5acd10146f42a0dd64a3326ea7e53e07d4915633.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/example-11036.json" "file_sha256" "c441ca84987a4a47d8f63d29751a15a52a25bf1c8239fdac4d727ffd70fa9a9a"} {"question" "e-11036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq  b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x \\lt  2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x}{45}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{45}\\,{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}({3}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/example-11036.json" "file_sha256" "c441ca84987a4a47d8f63d29751a15a52a25bf1c8239fdac4d727ffd70fa9a9a"} {"question" "e-11038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P\\left( 2 \\leq          X \\leq          4 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/assets/e01b36a6a2b00b47ce36b59d5b3e1a4fea4cbc26b0b7d46d60e40638161982d8.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/example-11038.json" "file_sha256" "4ce114e04285a940642efc2c1c5459ecde70072fd62fc7266cdf0d485585b8d0"} {"question" "e-11038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\leq        X \\leq        b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 4) & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{9}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}(x-3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{18}{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{3}+{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-3x]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}[{3}^{2}-{2}^{2}]+([\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2}-3(4)]-[\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2}-3(3)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{18}-4+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/example-11038.json" "file_sha256" "4ce114e04285a940642efc2c1c5459ecde70072fd62fc7266cdf0d485585b8d0"}] "usage" {"e-11036" [] "q-86913" [] "e-11038" [] "e-10839" []} "basis" 1956 "retractions" [[17592186193216 :question/problem "Compute $P(2 < X < 8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$f(x) = {\\frac{1}{50}x,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$."] [17592186192299 :question/problem "Compute $P\\left(1 \\lt X \\lt 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n${\\frac{1}{18}(x^{2} - 1),\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$."] [17592186192299 :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$, then\n\n$$\nP(a \\lt X \\lt b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1 < X < 3) &= ∫_{1}^{3}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{18}(x^{2} - 1)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}∫_{1}^{3}(x^{2} - 1)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}[\\frac{1}{3}x^{3} - x]_{1}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}([\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3} - (3)] - [\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3} - (1)]) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}([9 - 3] - [\\frac{1}{3} - 1]) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}(6 + \\frac{2}{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18} \\cdot \\frac{20}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{10}{27}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186192339 :question/problem "Compute $P\\left(X \\leq 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n${\\frac{2x}{45},\\begin{vmatrix}2 \\le x \\le 7, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$."] [17592186192339 :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$, then\n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x \\lt 2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X \\le 3) &= ∫_{2}^{3}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x}{45}dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{45}x^{2}]_{2}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{45}(3^{2} - 2^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{45} \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186192340 :question/problem "Compute $P\\left(2 \\leq X \\leq 4 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n${\\frac{1}{9}x,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x < 3, \\\\ x - 3,\\end{vmatrix}3 \\le x \\le 4,; 0, \\mid otherwise$."] [17592186192340 :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$, then\n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(2 \\le X \\le 4) &= ∫_{2}^{4}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{9}xdx + ∫_{3}^{4}(x - 3)dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{18}x^{2}]_{2}^{3} + [\\frac{1}{2}x^{2} - 3x]_{3}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}[3^{2} - 2^{2}] + ([\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2} - 3(4)] - [\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2} - 3(3)]) \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{18} - 4 + \\frac{9}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{14}{18} \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186192085 17592186192086 17592186192087 17592186192088 17592186192089] "immutable_fields" [[17592186192084 :answer-field/correct] [17592186192084 :answer-field/id] [17592186192084 :answer-field/key] [17592186192084 :answer-field/type]] "no_